  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "VRChat has some split locks (atomic memory acces across cpu cache line boundaries)(https://www.sobyte.net/post/2022-05/split-locks/), which degrade performance.\n\nI noticed since I am playing on linux and the kernel reports these events to the system log (but it is probably not a problem isolated to linux as it is a cpu feature).\n\nI tested with a different proton version and options and the problem persisted, I also tested with proton on a different game and it did not report split locks, so I think it is specific to VRChat (might also be EAC or something idk).\n\nA friend of mine also reported it happening on their machine.\n\nI attached journald logs from when I executed vrchat for about a minute.\n\nThere are some split locks when starting the game, but the ones that continue to appear are all at the same address.\n\nOn a normal run of VRChat I would have my logs filled with split locks from VRChat.exe processes with increasing PIDs.",
